crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:13:26: error: `position` has no parameter `y`
   |
13 | a = derivative(position, y)(1 s)
   |                          ^ not a parameter of `position`
 4 | def position(t: s) -> m:
   |     -------- `position` is defined here
   = note: its parameter is `t`
   = help: differentiate with respect to a parameter: `derivative(position, t)`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:14:26: error: the second argument of `derivative` is the name of a parameter of `position`
   |
14 | b = derivative(position, 0)(1 s)
   |                          ^ not a parameter name
 4 | def position(t: s) -> m:
   |     -------- `position` is defined here
   = help: write the parameter's name, not its position: `derivative(position, t)`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:15:23: error: cannot differentiate `loose`: its parameter `t` has no unit
   |
15 | c = derivative(loose, k)(1 s)
   |                       ^ while differentiating with respect to `k`
 7 | def loose(t, k: m) -> m:
   |     ----- `loose` is defined here
   = note: the derivative is computed through every parameter, so each needs a unit to type it
   = help: annotate the parameter with its unit, for example `t: s`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:16:23: error: cannot differentiate `loose` with respect to `t`: it has no unit
   |
16 | d = derivative(loose, t)(1 s)
   |                       ^ `t` is not annotated
 7 | def loose(t, k: m) -> m:
   |     ----- `loose` is defined here
   = note: the derivative has the unit of the result divided by the unit of `t`, and an unannotated parameter accepts any unit
   = help: annotate the parameter with its unit, for example `t: s`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:17:16: error: `derivative` needs a function defined with `def`, found the built-in `sqrt`
   |
17 | e = derivative(sqrt, x)(4)
   |                ^^^^ a built-in function
   = note: a `def` states the units of its parameters and result, which the unit of the derivative is computed from
   = help: wrap it in a `def` that states its units, and differentiate that

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:18:5: error: `derivative` takes 2 arguments, found 1: a function and the name of its parameter
   |
18 | f = derivative(position)(1 s)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ missing argument
   = help: write `derivative(f, x)(...)`, then the arguments of `f`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:19:16: error: `derivative` needs a function defined with `def`
   |
19 | g = derivative(3 m, t)(1 s)
   |                ^^^ this is length
   = help: define the function with `def f(x: unit) -> unit: ...` and differentiate that

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:20:16: error: cannot differentiate `shift` with respect to `p`: the derivative of an array with respect to an array is a Jacobian
   |
20 | h = derivative(shift, p)([1 m, 2 m, 3 m])
   |                ^^^^^ this function's result
10 | def shift(p: Vector[3] m) -> Vector[3] m:
   |     ----- `shift` is defined here
   = note: the result is Vector[3] [L], so the derivative would have an entry for every result and every entry of `p`, and Sky does not have Jacobians yet
   = help: differentiate a scalar result (a component, a norm, an energy) with respect to `p`, or an array result with respect to a scalar

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:21:16: error: `derivative` needs a function defined with `def`, found another derivative
   |
21 | j = derivative(derivative(position, t), t)(1 s)
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `derivative(...)`, which can only be called
   = help: name the first derivative with a `def` that calls it, and differentiate that

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_derivative_forms.sky:22:5: error: `derivative(position, t)` is a function, and must be called where it is written
   |
22 | k = derivative(position, t)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not called
   = note: Sky has no function values yet: a function can be called, but not stored or passed around
   = help: pass the arguments of the function: `derivative(position, t)(...)`, or name the derivative with a `def` that calls it
